 ## Background
-LODTree was introduced in the context of dynamic isosurface extraction and level-of-detail in voxel space [S1, unofficial]. It was developed to address storage overhead concerns in large volumetric datasets, leveraging bit-mapped cell data representation and virtual voxel expansion to achieve compact storage [S1, unofficial]. The method is discussed in relation to its performance compared to static geometry representations for isosurfaces [S1, unofficial].
